  "title": "Your possible pasts",
  "artist": "Pink Floyd",
  "genre": "unknown",
  "original_lyrics": "[verse]\nThey flutter behind you your possible pasts,\nSome brighteyed and crazy, some frightened and lost.\nwarning to anyone still in command\nOf their possible future, to take care.\n\n[intro]\nWith cattle trucks lying in wait for the next time.\nDo you remember me, how we used to be,\nDo you think we shoud be closer?\nShe stood in the doorway, the ghost of smile\nHaunting her face like cheap hotel sign.\nHer cold eyes imploring the men in their macs\nFor the gold in their bags or the knives in their backs.\nStepping up boldly one put out his hand.\nHe said, \"I was just child then, now I'm only man.\"\nDo you remember me, how we used to be,\nDo you think we should be closer?\n\n[bridge]\nShown how to feel good and told to feel bad.\nStrung out behind us the banners and flags\nOf our possible pasts lie in tatters and rags.\nDo you remember me, how we used to be,\nDo you think we should be closer?",
